-- REJECTED (§8.11). R11 elides a STRING field that nothing inspects, which
-- makes the emitted `P` narrower than its L4 source. Whole-record equality
-- reads every field implicitly, so the emitted `(a = b)` compares the narrowed
-- structures and answers `true` where L4 answers `false`. §8.11 conditions the
-- elision on the string being "never compared"; this compares it.

DECLARE P HAS name IS A STRING
              age  IS A NUMBER

@export
GIVEN a IS A P
      b IS A P
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
same a b MEANS a EQUALS b

#EVAL same OF (P WITH name IS "x", age IS 1), (P WITH name IS "y", age IS 1)   -- FALSE in L4
